---
term: Anti-capture protection
section: evolution-and-protection
order: 90
definition: An entrenched charter provision that stops any group from taking permanent control of a corporation or of its constitutional process.
seeAlso:
  - fundamental-protections
  - exit
  - living-charter
---
The most important anti-capture protections guarantee the following:

- Freedom to join and leave
- Prevention of permanent voting capture
- Prevention of incumbents controlling future membership
- Genuine democratic authority over charter evolution
- Protection against self-perpetuating political structures

These protections guard the constitutional process itself. They don't freeze any substantive policy.
